# Qarta Pay keeps one env file per workspace. Each has its own example with dummy values:
#
#   apps/api/.env.example    -> copy to apps/api/.env         (Reloadly test creds, dev keys, limits)
#   apps/web/.env.example    -> copy to apps/web/.env.local   (public NEXT_PUBLIC_ values only)
#   contracts/.env.example   -> copy to contracts/.env        (RPC URLs, public addresses, sweep settings)
#
# Real .env files are git-ignored. Private keys for deploys and the treasury sweep never go in
# any .env file: use Foundry's encrypted keystore. See docs/11-SECURITY-AND-SECRETS.md.
